      "content": "It takes immense strength to recognize how your presence is affecting those you care about, even if that recognition is steeped in despair. Those feelings of being a burden are a sign of how much you care about them, but they are distortions of reality, not facts. You are not a burden; you are a person, and your needs matter just as much as anyone else's. Please consider talking to a therapist who can help you process these overwhelming feelings of guilt and self-worth.",
